WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.650
Bangkok, in Thailand, had about
18 million people in 2025.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.310
Look for a second Thai city on the
UN's list of cities above 5 million.

3
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.750
There isn't one.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.510
Cross to the USA.

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:20.110
New York had about 13.9 million people,
and Los Angeles about 12.7 million.

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.470
Why does one country
have a single giant city,

7
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.830
while the other has many large ones?

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.350
In this mission, you'll test a rule that
predicts how big a country's second,

9
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.990
third and fourth cities should be.

10
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.490
Then you'll find out why
big cities lie far apart,

11
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.370
while small towns sit close together.

12
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.250
Your mission: explain why Thailand and
the USA have such different patterns of

13
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.010
cities.
